  "notes": {
    "omitted-root": "Kotlin allows the directory layout to omit the common root package: src/main/kotlin/Main.kt is package com.acme.notes, src/main/kotlin/data/ is com.acme.notes.data, and so on. Test sources under src/test/kotlin follow the same omission.",
    "one-line-classes": "util/Clock.kt and tags/TagModels.kt put two classes on adjacent lines, each with a one-line body (`class Clock { fun now(): Long = ... }`), the second with a modifier (`internal class`, `data class`). All their classes and functions must be extracted (see `symbols`). `Clock().now()` in Stopwatch.elapsed is Clock.now in the same file (Clock() is a constructor call, not listed).",
    "string-template": "`\"Created ${ slugify(note.title) } at ${formatStamp(note.createdAt)}\"`: calls inside `${ }` (with and without inner spaces) are real calls.",
    "same-package-top-level": "formatStamp is a top-level function in Format.kt, package com.acme.notes (same package as Main.kt): no import needed.",
    "top-level-import": "`import com.acme.notes.util.slugify` / `truncate` / `com.acme.notes.report.runReport` import top-level functions; the compiler binds each to the one file that declares it (util/Text.kt, report/Report.kt). IMPORTS goes to that file.",
    "extension-import": "`note.isStale(now)` looks like a member call but Note has no isStale member; it is the extension function imported by `import com.acme.notes.data.isStale`, declared in data/NoteExt.kt.",
    "wildcard": "`import com.acme.notes.util.*` brings in slugify and truncate (Text.kt); IMPORTS lists every file of that package (Text.kt, Clock.kt).",
    "primary-ctor-property": "`class NoteRepository(private val clock: Clock = Clock())`: `clock.now()` is Clock.now.",
    "typed-local": "`val repo = NoteRepository()` / `val tags = TagSet()` type the locals.",
    "typed-param": "`repo: NoteRepository` parameter.",
    "stdlib-collection": "`notes.add(note)` / `tags.add(...)` are MutableList/MutableSet.add. TagSet.add calling tags.add must not self-loop, and NoteRepository.create's notes.add must not link to TagSet.add.",
    "test-same-package": "Test files declare the same package as the code under test, so no import is needed.",
    "scope": "Constructor calls (`Note(...)`, `Clock()`, `TagSet()`, `MarkdownExporter()`) are not listed as calls. Lambda bodies contain no repo calls. .kts build scripts are not source."
  }
